==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory|Gories]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Master A.]] spawns.
**1 [[Dagshund]] spawns.
**1 [[Dagshund]] spawns.

==Strategy==
At the start, spam [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cats]]. After that, this stage becomes trivially easy with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]]. If Bahamut cat is not owned, [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]] can be used instead. Just remember to bring meatshields.

==Trivia==
*Going along with the "risqué" theme of [[Risqué Terrain]], Lovely Minerals' Japanese name, Porori Kōseki (ぽろり鉱石), would appear to carry the same exact meaning as the English name. However, ''Porori'' is also a slang term for an instance of a woman's nipple briefly being exposed - a "nip slip".

